{
  "title": "Dua-e-Noor",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "In Muhaj al-Da’awat, Sayyid Ibn Tawus has mentioned a narration quoting Salman as saying, “Lady Fatimah al-Zahra’(a.s.) conveyed to me some words that she had learnt from the Holy Messenger (s.a.w.a.) and she used to repeat them each morning and evening. Moreover, she said that if you would like not to be afflicted by the harm of fever as long as you live in this world, you may say this supplicatory prayer regularly:\nبِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nIn the Name of Allah, the Most Compassionate, the Most Merciful.\nبِسْمِ اللهِ النُّوْرِ\nBISMIL LAAHIN NOOR\nIn the Name of Allah, the Light (Nur).\nبِسْمِ اللهِ نُوْرِ النُّوْرِ\nBISMIL LAAHIN NOORIN NOOR\nIn the Name of Allah, the Light of the Light.\nبِسْمِ اللهِ نُوْرٌ عَلٰى نُوْرٍ\nBISMIL LAAHIN NOORE A’LAA NOORIN\nIn the Name of Allah, Light upon Light.\nبِسْمِ اللهِ الَّذِيْ هُوَ مُدَبِّرُ الْاُمُوْرِ\nBISMIL LAAHIL LAZEE HOWA MODABBERUL OMOORE\nIn the Name of Allah, Who is the Controller of all Affairs.\nبِسْمِ اللهِ خَلَقَ النُّوْرَ مِنَ النُّوْرِ\nBISMIL LAAHE KHAALEQIN NOORE MENAN NOOR\nIn the Name of Allah, Who created the Light from the Light.\nاَلْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِيْ خَلَقَ النُّوْرَ مِنَ النُّوْرِ\nALHAMDO LILLAAHIL LAZEE KHALAQAN NOORA MENAN NOORE\nPraise be to Allah, Who created the Light from the Light, \nوَ اَنْزَلَ النُّوْرَ عَلَى الطُّوْرِ\nWA ANZALAN NOORA A’LAT TOORE\nand sent down the Light upon [Mount] Tur (Sinai),\nفِيْ كِتَابٍ مَّسْطُوْرٍ\nFEE KETAABIM MASTOORIN\nin a written book, \nفِيْ رَقٍّ مَّنْشُوْرٍ\nFEE RAQQIM MANSHOORIN\non an open scroll, \nبِقَدَرٍ مَّقْدُوْرٍ\nBE-QADARIM MAQDOORIN\nwith a measured decree, \nعَلٰى نَبِيٍّ مَّحْبُوْرٍ\nA’LAA NABIYYIM MAHBOORIN\nupon a Prophet who is honored.\nاَلْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِيْ هُوَ بِالْعِزِّ مَذْكُوْرٌ\nALHAMDO LILLAAHIL LAZEE HOWA BIL 'IZZIM MAZKOORUN\nPraise be to Allah, Who is mentioned with Glory, \nوَ بِالْفَخْرِ مَشْهُوْرٌ\nWA BIL-FAKHRE MASHHOORUN\nand known with Honor, \nوَ عَلَى السَّرَّآءِ وَ الضَّرَّآءِ مَشْكُوْرٌ\nWA A’LAS SARRAAAE WAZ ZARRAAAE MASHKOORUN\nand thanked both in ease and in hardship.\nوَ صَلَّى اللهُ عَلٰى سَيِّدِنَا مُحَمَّدٍ\nWA SALLAL LAAHO A’LAA SAYYEDENAA MOHAMMADINW\nAnd may Allah bless our Master Muhammad \nوَّ آلِهِ الطَّاهِرِيْنَ.\nWA AALEHIT TAAHEREENA.\nand his pure progeny.\nSalman then added, “As I learnt by heart these words, I conveyed them to more than one thousand persons in al-Madinah and Makkah who had been infected with fever and they all were healed by the will of Almighty Allah."
}
